## Summary

Error-aware `/run` — offer to analyze failures

### Changes made:

1. **`src/commands_run.rs`** — Core implementation:
   • Added RunResult struct with exit_code, stdout, stderr, elapsed, success fields
   • Refactored run_shell_command to return RunResult while preserving real-time streaming (stdout/stderr still print line-by-line via threads, but also collect into Vec<String> buffers)
   • Added LAST_FAILED_RUN static Mutex<Option<RunResult>> with `get_last_failed_run(), set_last_failed_run(), clear_last_failed_run() — all using lock_or_recover` for poison-safe access
   • Added print_run_result() that shows: on success → ✓ exit 0 (elapsed); on failure → `✗ exit N (elapsed)` + up to 3 lines of stderr preview + error-like stdout lines + a hint: `💡 Command failed. Ask me to analyze the error, or say /fix to auto-fix.`
   • Updated handle_run to use RunResult, store failures, clear on success
   • 8 new tests covering: successful result fields, failure result fields, multiline capture, last-failed-run lifecycle (initial None, store/retrieve, clear), print_run_result for both success and failure

2. `src/commands_dev.rs` — /fix integration:
   • handle_fix now calls `get_last_failed_run() and appends the last failed /run` output (stderr + stdout) to the fix prompt, giving the AI richer diagnostic context

3. **`docs/src/usage/commands.md** — Updated /run` docs to mention the error analysis hint

